@startuml MCP Integration Workflow

!theme plain
title SABER MCP Integration - Connection-Based Session Mapping (MCP Compliant)

actor Agent
participant "ServerClient" as Client
participant "SessionRestAPI\n(REST)" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI\n(MCP Component)" as MCP
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "TaskManager" as TM

== Session Initialization ==
Agent -> Client: initialize()
Client -> REST: POST /session
REST -> SM: create_session()
SM -> Client: session_id

== MCP Connection with Headers ==
Agent -> Client: connect_mcp_with_headers()
note right: Headers: X-SABER-Session-ID, X-SABER-Task-ID, X-SABER-Client-ID
Client -> MCP: connect(headers)
MCP -> MCP: _handle_mcp_connection(connection_id, headers)
MCP -> SM: create_session() or map_existing_session()
MCP -> SM: start_episode(task_id) if provided
MCP -> MCP: map connection_id → session_id
MCP -> Client: mcp_connected

== Tool Discovery (Clean MCP Tools) ==
Agent -> Client: get_available_tools()
Client -> MCP: list_tools()
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM_EXEC: to_mcp_tools()
note right of EM_EXEC: Returns clean tool schemas:\n- execute_python(code)\n- execute_cli(command)\n- end_episode(submission)
EM_EXEC -> MCP: clean_tool_schemas[]
MCP -> Client: mcp_tools[]
Client -> Agent: available_tools[]

== Command Execution (No Session Context in Tools) ==
Agent -> Client: execute_python(code="print('hello')")
Client -> MCP: call_tool("execute_python", {code: "print('hello')"})
MCP -> MCP: get_session_from_connection(connection_id)
MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, action)
note right of MCP: Session context handled\nat connection level,\nnot in tool parameters
SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action, context)
EM_EXEC -> SM: command_result
SM -> EM_EP: step(session_id, action, result)
EM_EP -> SM: step_result
SM -> MCP: execution_result
MCP -> Client: mcp_result
Client -> Agent: command_result

== Episode End (Clean Tool) ==
Agent -> Client: end_episode(submission="flag{found}")
Client -> MCP: call_tool("end_episode", {submission: "flag{found}"})
MCP -> MCP: get_session_from_connection(connection_id)
MCP -> SM: end_episode(session_id, submission)
SM -> MCP: episode_ended
MCP -> Client: success_result
Client -> Agent: episode_completed

== Session Cleanup ==
Agent -> Client: disconnect_mcp()
MCP -> MCP: _cleanup_connection(connection_id)
MCP -> SM: terminate_session(session_id)
Client -> REST: DELETE /session/{id} (optional)
REST -> SM: terminate_session() (if needed)

note right of MCP
**MCP Compliance Achieved**
✅ Clean tool schemas (no session_id)
✅ Connection-based session mapping
✅ Pure functional parameters
✅ Standard MCP client compatibility
✅ Semantic parameter names

**Tool Examples:**
- execute_python(code: str)
- execute_cli(command: str)
- end_episode(submission?: str)
end note

note right of REST
**SessionRestAPI Responsibilities**
- Session lifecycle management
- Episode management
- Policy access
- Status monitoring
- Event streaming
- Health checks
end note

note right of SM
**Dual Protocol Support**
- REST API for session management
- MCP API for tool execution
- Connection → Session mapping
- Automatic session creation
- Resource cleanup on disconnect
end note

@enduml
